-- Migration 1 -> 2.
--
-- This file exists to establish the mechanism, not because the index is urgent.
--
-- Before it, this kit had NO .sqm files, so SQLDelight's generated schema version never moved.
-- Adding a table to a .sq file therefore reached new installs only: on an existing database neither
-- create() nor migrate() runs, the table is silently absent, the first write throws inside the
-- persist step, the kit (correctly) refuses to ack — and that device then receives nothing, ever
-- again, while the server prunes at 1000 messages / 30 days. Silent and permanent.
--
-- Phase 3 both ADDS tables (the inbox) and DELETES them (ORM entries, model config), so the reset
-- cannot proceed safely without this. See obscura-proto/KIT_API.md P1.
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS friend_status_idx ON Friend(status);
